          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Which chapter holds high blood pressure, and what does that chapter deliberately exclude?",
          "answer": "The information regarding high blood pressure can be found in the chapter related to the ICD-10 coding for hypertension, specifically the document titled \"Coding hypertension: I10 and the hypertensive disease family.\" \n\nThis chapter deliberately excludes specific conditions and circumstances. Notably, it states that:\n\n1. A single raised blood pressure reading without a diagnosis of hypertension is considered an abnormal finding rather than a disease, and it is classified under Chapter 18, which deals with abnormal findings.\n2. Hypertension complicating pregnancy, childbirth, or the postpartum period is excluded outright and is classified in the obstetric chapter.\n3. Hypertension affecting the vessels of the brain or eye is also addressed separately and may be coded in addition to hypertension, rather than with the I10 code.\n\nThese exclusions clarify the contexts in which hypertension is classified and treated within the coding system, ensuring accurate documentation based on clinical diagnosis (source: \"Coding hypertension: I10 and the hypertensive disease family\").\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
